  "sharing_rule": "Exact original reference and rendered presentation. Existing external portrait family aliases omit only unused fallback ornaments; project atlases remain strict.",
  "authoring_instructions": "{\"original\":\"Create a complete 2D isometric RPG animation atlas derived strictly from the attached original character. Preserve this exact original design, proportions, palette, face, equipment and anatomy. Keep the same detailed small painted game sprite style and elevated isometric viewpoint. Transparent RGBA background, no scenery, labels or grid. Exactly EIGHT COLUMNS and THIRTEEN ROWS, exactly 104 whole separate articulated poses. Columns left to right are E screen-right profile, SE front-right, S full front, SW front-left, W screen-left profile, NW back-left, N full back, NE back-right. Back views must show the actual back with no front face visible. Maintain those directions in every row. Make each whole pose SMALL relative to its cell: only 50 percent of the cell width and height including extended limbs/weapon/tail. At least 25 pixels of fully transparent gutter on every side, plus generous outside margin. No overlap or edge clipping. Consistent body scale. Thirteen rows exactly: 1 idle neutral; 2 distinct breathing idle; 3 walking first step; 4 walking passing stance; 5 walking opposite step; 6 attack windup; 7 actual attack contact in the facing direction; 8 attack recovery; 9 hit recoil; 10 recover from hit; 11 death begins buckling down; 12 falling close to floor; 13 fully collapsed flat corpse. Articulate body and limbs into real distinct animation poses, no copied/translated stills. Death keeps the recognizable body contiguous with limbs connected. Use the original COCKATRICE creature exactly: olive-green scaly reptile body and thick tail, shaggy pale gray/white mane around its rooster-like head, red comb on the crown, ochre curved beak, original clawed limbs and feet. Preserve its exact existing animal anatomy and limb count; do not turn it into a human, a giant chicken, a conventional winged dragon or a different lizard. No added equipment or invented wings. Its attack winds the head/body back, then lunges and pecks/bites with the original beak in the facing direction, then recovers. Walk using its original legs and balance the original tail; tail stays connected and completely inside its cell. The death ends as this recognizable animal lying flat with folded limbs. No particles or glow.\",\"south_contact_correction\":\"Correct ONE pose in this existing transparent cockatrice sheet, retaining the original character and every other pose. The problem is the THIRD COLUMN of the SEVENTH ROW, the south/front ATTACK CONTACT. That pose wrongly turns into a right profile. Redraw only that pose as the same animal viewed DIRECTLY FROM FRONT, lunging/pecking toward the viewer (screen-down), with the beak in front of the chest and centered between both shoulders, symmetrical frontal view, BOTH sides of its face visible. Its red comb should run vertically up the centered head; its two eyes flank the beak, its tail is behind the body and not sticking left/right in profile. It should be a dynamic forward biting contact, head lowered toward camera, consistent with the FRONT idle poses above and below in this same third column. Do not face right or left. Preserve exact olive-green body, red comb, gray mane and original limbs. Keep the other 103 poses, the complete eight-column thirteen-row grid, all spacing, transparency and overall body scale unchanged. Do not add particles, shadows, labels, weapons or a background. Only fix that south contact facing direction.\"}",
  "instruction_record_kind": "exact_original_and_facing_correction_prompts",
